{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772651002,"nonce":"FcgUB/Jj7vJYg/lyE3GAOOJGlwY=","title":"Auth request: post-merge handoff note (context dump for merge completion)","message":"Allow agents to attach a \"post-merge handoff\" note when submitting an auth request. When the merge completes successfully, this note is delivered as an inbox item in the next session.\n\n## Motivation\nCurrently auth result inbox items just say \"merge X completed.\" The agent that originally submitted the request may have had important loose ends or follow-up context. That context lives in the conversation that has since ended.\n\nThe handoff note would contain: a compressed summary of state after the merge, any pending follow-ups that depend on the merge succeeding, and minimal context needed for a fresh session to continue intelligently.\n\n## Design\n- Add `post_merge_handoff TEXT` field to auth_requests table (migration)\n- API: accept `post_merge_handoff` in POST/PUT body\n- auth-merge: if present, include in the inbox item created on successful merge\n\nMigrated from dotfiles issue a065ad7.","files":null}]}